<title>UK: Whitbread says trading good, meets forecast.</title>
<headline>Whitbread says trading good, meets forecast.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brewer to leisure group Whitbread Plc gave a rosy outlook on Wednesday, with chairman Sir Michael Angus saying trading continued to be &quot;robust&quot; in the new financial year and was in line with its forecasts.</p>
<p>He added the company planned no new major acquisitions in the coming year but would focus instead on selling off its poorer assets and organic growth.</p>
<p>His remarks were attached to the group's 1996 results which showed a 12 percent increase in pretax, pre-exceptional profits to 316.5 million pounds.</p>
</text>
